/// How urgent an incoming email is for the project manager. Critical means the email changes or threatens the completion date, the budget, the scope or a contract clause and needs action now. Watch means nothing changes today but the email could affect schedule, cost or scope later, for example when the customer announces an absence, a delay of their own or a vague wish. Not critical means routine information that has no effect on schedule, cost, scope or contract, for example a status meeting or a request for an existing document.
rule EmailCriticality
	lineageTag: 715b2ef6-b7f8-5506-a153-11dcf03bf6a2
	statement: An email is critical if it affects the completion date, the budget or the scope of its project, or if it contradicts an assumption or clause in the specification, offer or contract of that project. An email that only needs to be monitored is rated watch. All other emails are rated not critical.
	ruleReferencedEntity Email
	ruleReferencedEntity ProjectDocument
	ruleReferencedRelationship 'Email About Project'
	ruleReferencedRelationship 'Document Of Project'
